"The help"?

48
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.634
MARTA: It's okay.
I'm sorry.

49
00:04:12.636 --> 00:04:15.172
No. it's not okay.
What the hell?

50
00:04:15.938 --> 00:04:17.107
(SIGHS)

51
00:04:17.641 --> 00:04:18.908
Aw.

52
00:04:24.947 --> 00:04:26.083
How are
you doing?

53
00:04:28.085 --> 00:04:29.418
Not very good.

54
00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.421
Alone.

55
00:04:31.388 --> 00:04:35.125
Lots of this and not
knowing what to do next.

56
00:04:36.093 --> 00:04:39.927
Marta. anything
you need...

57
00:04:39.929 --> 00:04:41.432
You're part of
this family.

58
00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:44.601
Thank you.

59
00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.403
- How you doing. kiddo?
- MARTA: Linda.

60
00:04:48.405 --> 00:04:50.605
- (MAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)
- How are you?

61
00:04:50.607 --> 00:04:52.541
(SIGHS)

62
00:04:52.543 --> 00:04:56.144
You know. the funeral helped. I guess.
Just seeing him.

63
00:04:56.146 --> 00:04:58.045
I thought you should
have been there.

64
00:04:58.047 --> 00:05:00.014
- I was outvoted.
- RICHARD: Get arrested!

65
00:05:00.016 --> 00:05:02.319
- Die up your own ass for all I care!
- Richard.

66
00:05:03.454 --> 00:05:05.055
- (PHONE BEEPS)
- He's not coming.

67
00:05:05.955 --> 00:05:07.622
Ransom. Little shit.

68
00:05:07.624 --> 00:05:08.625
Missed the funeral.

69
00:05:09.293 --> 00:05:10.958
WAGNER: Excuse me.

70
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.361
Uh. we're ready
for you now.

71
00:05:12.363 --> 00:05:14.096
We'd like to see you
one at a time.

72
00:05:14.098 --> 00:05:16.331
LINDA: All right.
Uh. I'll go first.

73
00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:18.367
I'm assuming this
will all be wrapped up

74
00:05:18.369 --> 00:05:20.168
before the
memorial tonight.

75
00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.670
WAGNER: We'll do
our best. ma'am.

76
00:05:21.672 --> 00:05:23.171
(SIGHS)

77
00:05:23.173 --> 00:05:24.473
(DOOR CLOSES)

78
00:05:24.475 --> 00:05:26.074
So...

79
00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:28.677
How you
doing. kiddo?

80
00:05:28.679 --> 00:05:31.413
We're just gonna reintroduce
ourselves as a formality.

81
00:05:31.415 --> 00:05:33.181
I am Detective
Lieutenant Elliot.

82
00:05:33.183 --> 00:05:34.716
and this is
Trooper Wagner.

83
00:05:34.718 --> 00:05:38.186
Now. um.
I'm going to record this.

84
00:05:38.188 --> 00:05:40.155
just to make things easier.

85
00:05:40.157 --> 00:05:43.725
All right. we're with
Linda Drysdale nee Thrombey.

86
00:05:43.727 --> 00:05:45.594
Harlan Thrombey's
eldest daughter.

87
00:05:45.596 --> 00:05:47.329
and discussing
the events that took place

88
00:05:47.331 --> 00:05:49.398
the night of his demise
one week ago.

89
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.699
November eighth.

90
00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:52.536
We're very sorry
for your loss.

91
00:05:54.104 --> 00:05:56.705
Thank you.
That means a lot.

92
00:05:56.707 --> 00:05:58.640
So. we understand
on that night

93
00:05:58.642 --> 00:06:00.075
the family had gathered

94
00:06:00.077 --> 00:06:02.144
to celebrate your
father's 85th birthday?

95
00:06:02.146 --> 00:06:03.412
Yes.

96
00:06:03.414 --> 00:06:06.214
- How was it? Uh...
- LINDA: The party?

97
00:06:06.216 --> 00:06:07.451
Pre-my-dad's-death?

98
00:06:08.218 --> 00:06:10.185
Oh. it was great.

99
00:06:10.187 --> 00:06:12.454
Did anyone besides
the family show face?

100
00:06:12.456 --> 00:06:15.157
LINDA: <i>Um. Fran.
the housekeeper.</i>

101
00:06:15.159 --> 00:06:18.126
He was a nice guy.
but he was so hairy.

102
00:06:18.128 --> 00:06:20.195
- WALT: Jacob?
- And I've dated Italian guys.

103
00:06:20.197 --> 00:06:22.063
You know what I mean?
It was like...

104
00:06:22.065 --> 00:06:24.499
LINDA: <i>Marta.
Harlan's caregiver.</i>

105
00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:26.635
<i>Good girl. Hard worker.</i>

106
00:06:26.637 --> 00:06:28.205
Her family's from Ecuador.

107
00:06:29.106 --> 00:06:30.705
And Wanetta.

108
00:06:30.707 --> 00:06:33.074
<i>Great nana. Harlan's mom.</i>

109
00:06:33.076 --> 00:06:35.410
- Hi. Nana.
- ELLIOTT: <i>His mom?</i>

110
00:06:35.412 --> 00:06:37.612
- Nana?
- ELLIOTT: <i>Wow. How old is she?</i>

111
00:06:37.614 --> 00:06:39.414
LINDA: <i>We have no idea.</i>

112
00:06:39.416 --> 00:06:41.583
Okay. um.
and your son. Ransom.

113
00:06:41.585 --> 00:06:43.385
<i>did he attend as well?</i>

114
00:06:43.387 --> 00:06:45.155
LINDA: <i>Yes. but he left early.</i>

115
00:06:45.789 --> 00:06:49.293
Ransom. are you leaving?

116
00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:50.993
(PLAYS NOTE)

117
00:06:54.198 --> 00:06:55.464
Right. um...

118
00:06:55.466 --> 00:06:57.199
Would you say that
all three of you showed up

119
00:06:57.201 --> 00:06:58.368
