120
00:06:59.369 --> 00:07:00.704
No.

121
00:07:03.039 --> 00:07:06.575
Richard came early
to help the caterers set up.

122
00:07:06.577 --> 00:07:08.543
Okay. And you and
your husband. Richard.

123
00:07:08.545 --> 00:07:10.178
work at a real estate
firm in Boston?

124
00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.447
No. It's...
It's my company.

125
00:07:12.449 --> 00:07:14.082
Right. Right. Sorry.

126
00:07:14.084 --> 00:07:15.784
I built my business
from the ground up.

127
00:07:15.786 --> 00:07:17.752
Oh. just like your father.

128
00:07:17.754 --> 00:07:20.422
You two were very close.

129
00:07:20.424 --> 00:07:23.792
We... We had our own secret
way of communicating.

130
00:07:23.794 --> 00:07:27.162
I mean. you had to
find that with Dad.

131
00:07:27.164 --> 00:07:29.197
You had to find a game
to play with him.

132
00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:32.636
and if you did that.
and you played by his rules...

133
00:07:38.475 --> 00:07:41.176
Everyone idolizes
their dad. right?

134
00:07:41.178 --> 00:07:42.679
I don't know.
Do they?

135
00:07:44.081 --> 00:07:45.847
Very much not.

136
00:07:45.849 --> 00:07:47.716
Don't know why
I said that.

137
00:07:47.718 --> 00:07:50.118
<i>But my wife. Linda. does.</i>

138
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.487
<i>Harlan started out
with a rusty Smith Corona</i>

139
00:07:52.489 --> 00:07:53.822
<i>and built himself into</i>

140
00:07:53.824 --> 00:07:56.758
<i>one of the best-selling
mystery writers of all time.</i>

141
00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:01.131
Wow. seems like all his kids
are self-made overachievers.

142
00:08:02.766 --> 00:08:03.932
(SIGHS) Sure.

143
00:08:03.934 --> 00:08:06.568
ELLIOTT: For the record.
I'm speaking with Walt Thrombey.

144
00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:09.237
Harlan Thrombey's
youngest son.

145
00:08:09.239 --> 00:08:11.740
So. you run your father's
publishing company?

146
00:08:11.742 --> 00:08:14.276
Yeah. It's my...
It's our...

147
00:08:14.278 --> 00:08:16.344
Uh. it's the family's
publishing company.

148
00:08:16.346 --> 00:08:17.581
Dad trusts me to run it.

149
00:08:18.749 --> 00:08:20.415
Thirty languages.

150
00:08:20.417 --> 00:08:24.286
Over 80 million copies sold.
A real legacy.

151
00:08:24.288 --> 00:08:26.154
- ELLIOTT: Mmm-hmm.
- You guys fans?

152
00:08:26.156 --> 00:08:28.690
I mean. I don't do much
fiction reading myself. but...

153
00:08:28.692 --> 00:08:30.392
Big fan.
I'm a big fan.

154
00:08:30.394 --> 00:08:32.594
I mean.
his plots are just like...

155
00:08:32.596 --> 00:08:33.862
Like. I won't
spoil it for you but...

156
00:08:33.864 --> 00:08:35.530
Okay. like
<i>Thousand Knives?</i>

157
00:08:35.532 --> 00:08:36.865
<i>The Cow
