202
00:10:24.007 --> 00:10:25.373
That's Flam.

203
00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:27.308
But it's also Harlan.

204
00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.778
He got me and Meg
through some tough times.

205
00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:31.379
Grandad gives my mom
a yearly allowance

206
00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:32.814
and he's never missed wiring

207
00:10:32.816 --> 00:10:34.851
a tuition payment
to my schools.

208
00:10:36.987 --> 00:10:39.821
He's a genuinely
selfless man.

209
00:10:39.823 --> 00:10:41.890
But you left
the party early?

210
00:10:41.892 --> 00:10:42.957
MEG: Have fun.

211
00:10:42.959 --> 00:10:44.259
<i>To see some friends at Smith.</i>

212
00:10:44.261 --> 00:10:46.027
You know Dad pays for her

213
00:10:46.029 --> 00:10:49.964
crypto-Marxist-post-
deconstructural-

214
00:10:49.966 --> 00:10:53.268
feminist-poetry-theory-
whatever major?

215
00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.570
She could have stuck
around for the cake.

216
00:10:55.572 --> 00:10:57.340
JONI: <i>I think Linda was upset.</i>

217
00:10:58.809 --> 00:10:59.910
Hmm.

218
00:11:01.278 --> 00:11:02.713
But Harlan understood.

219
00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.482
(PLAYS NOTE ON PIANO)

220
00:11:07.051 --> 00:11:08.349
Right.

221
00:11:08.351 --> 00:11:11.820
Um. you two showed up to the
party around the same time...

222
00:11:11.822 --> 00:11:13.988
If I could pause?

223
00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:14.991
Because I just...

224
00:11:15.892 --> 00:11:17.392
Who is that guy?

225
00:11:17.394 --> 00:11:19.327
And why are we doing
all this again? (CHUCKLES)

226
00:11:19.329 --> 00:11:20.628
ELLIOTT: This is just some
follow-up questions.

227
00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.064
Um. we're attempting
to be thorough.

228
00:11:22.066 --> 00:11:23.765
so we can figure out
the manner of death.

229
00:11:23.767 --> 00:11:25.366
So by "manner of death."

230
00:11:25.368 --> 00:11:26.835
you mean if
someone killed him?

231
00:11:26.837 --> 00:11:28.870
