243
00:11:49.659 --> 00:11:50.925
JONI: Wait a minute.

244
00:11:50.927 --> 00:11:54.096
I read a tweet about a
<i>New Yorker</i> article about you.

245
00:11:54.098 --> 00:11:56.598
"The Last
of the Gentlemen Sleuths."

246
00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.967
You solved that case
with the tennis champ?

247
00:11:58.969 --> 00:12:02.071
(CHUCKLES) You're famous.

248
00:12:02.073 --> 00:12:04.372
ELLIOTT: Mr. Blanc is not
with the police department

249
00:12:04.374 --> 00:12:05.974
and not officially involved
in the case.

250
00:12:05.976 --> 00:12:07.709
but he's offered to consult.

251
00:12:07.711 --> 00:12:10.044
Now. I happily obliged.
and I can vouch for him.

252
00:12:10.046 --> 00:12:11.946
Mr. Blanc.
I know who you are.

253
00:12:11.948 --> 00:12:13.882
I read your profile
in the <i>New Yorker.</i>

254
00:12:13.884 --> 00:12:16.384
I found it delightful.

255
00:12:16.386 --> 00:12:19.554
I just buried
my 85-year-old father

256
00:12:19.556 --> 00:12:21.523
who committed suicide.

257
00:12:21.525 --> 00:12:23.925
Why are you here?

258
00:12:23.927 --> 00:12:27.597
(CLICKS TONGUE) I'm here
at the behest of a client.

259
00:12:28.132 --> 00:12:29.366
Who?

260
00:12:30.634 --> 00:12:32.567
I cannot say.

261
00:12:32.569 --> 00:12:34.602
But let me assure you this.

262
00:12:34.604 --> 00:12:38.006
My presence
will be ornamental.

263
00:12:38.008 --> 00:12:40.775
You will find me a respectful.

264
00:12:40.777 --> 00:12:43.613
quiet. passive observer

265
00:12:44.714 --> 00:12:45.982
of the truth.

266
00:12:47.651 --> 00:12:49.017
Fine.

267
00:12:49.019 --> 00:12:50.518
Are we getting there?

268
00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.753
Nearly. Um...

269
00:12:51.755 --> 00:12:54.022
Harlan's nurse.
she was at the party

270
00:12:54.024 --> 00:12:55.990
in a professional capacity?

271
00:12:55.992 --> 00:12:56.993
Marta?

272
00:12:57.761 --> 00:12:58.927
I guess.

273
00:12:58.929 --> 00:13:01.163
<i>Harlan hired her
to be around to take care</i>

274
00:13:01.165 --> 00:13:03.565
<i>of whatever medical needs
popped up.</i>

275
00:13:03.567 --> 00:13:06.603
<i>But really.
she's like part of the family.</i>

276
00:13:07.003 --> 00:13:08.436
<i>Good kid.</i>

277
00:13:08.438 --> 00:13:10.072
<i>Been a good friend to Harlan.</i>

278
00:13:10.074 --> 00:13:12.006
<i>Family's from Paraguay.</i>

279
00:13:12.008 --> 00:13:14.078
Linda really likes
her work ethic.

280
00:13:15.612 --> 00:13:18.348
"Immigrants.
We get the job done."

281
00:13:20.917 --> 00:13:22.817
- (STUTTERS) I...
- From <i>Hamilton.</i>

282
00:13:22.819 --> 00:13:24.485
- WAGNER: Oh. <i>Hamilton.</i>
- (LAUGHS)

283
00:13:24.487 --> 00:13:25.620
It's so good.
It's so good.

284
00:13:25.622 --> 00:13:27.424
- I saw it at The Public.
- WAGNER: Oh!

285
00:13:28.825 --> 00:13:30.861
(STUTTERS)
May I just. um...

286
00:13:31.628 --> 00:13:33.828
Then I'll recede. but...

287
00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.899
As a self-made
man myself.

288
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.068
I have to express
my admiration

289
00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:41.671
for how you followed
in your father's footsteps.

290
00:13:43.506 --> 00:13:45.874
- Thank you.
- BENOIT: Just marvelous.

291
00:13:45.876 --> 00:13:47.909
You know.
the whole family. too.

292
00:13:47.911 --> 00:13:49.878
And Joni with her thing.

293
00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:52.480
and Walt with his
publishing empire...

294
00:13:52.482 --> 00:13:53.683
(STUTTERS) It's...

295
00:13:54.618 --> 00:13:55.619
Well...

296
00:13:56.987 --> 00:14:00.055
Yes. I mean. Walt.
he's done well

297
00:14:00.057 --> 00:14:02.557
with what Dad gave him.

298
00:14:02.559 --> 00:14:03.591
Not that it matters.

299
00:14:03.593 --> 00:14:06.661
But really. Dad hands him
a book twice a year

300
00:14:06.663 --> 00:14:07.831
and Walt publishes it.

301
00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.032
It's just not the same.

302
00:14:11.034 --> 00:14:15.237
But surely Walt runs the
merchandising. adaptations.

303
00:14:15.239 --> 00:14:17.472
film and television rights.
I mean...

304
00:14:17.474 --> 00:14:19.141
Are you baiting me. Detective?

305
00:14:19.143 --> 00:14:20.675
(STUTTERS)

306
00:14:20.677 --> 00:14:22.677
You know he doesn't.

307
00:14:22.679 --> 00:14:24.946
And if you think
I am dumb enough

308
00:14:24.948 --> 00:14:27.949
to be baited into
talking family business.

309
00:14:27.951 --> 00:14:30.518
into shit-talking
my baby brother.

310
00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:32.154
in front of
a police detective.

311
00:14:32.156 --> 00:14:33.688
and a state trooper...

312
00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.857
Walt doesn't run shit.

313
00:14:35.859 --> 00:14:38.526
Because there are no TV
and film rights.

314
00:14:38.528 --> 00:14:41.230
Harlan never allowed
any adaptations of his books.

315
00:14:41.232 --> 00:14:42.630
Hated the idea.

316
00:14:42.632 --> 00:14:43.731
No.

317
00:14:43.733 --> 00:14:44.999
Yeah!

318
00:14:45.001 --> 00:14:46.701
Drives Walt nuts.

319
00:14:46.703 --> 00:14:48.803
'Cause that's where
the real money is.

320
00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:51.173
When Walt would get
a little Irish courage in him.

321
00:14:51.175 --> 00:14:53.108
- <i>he'd get into it with Harlan.</i>
- The window is...

322
00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:55.578
Did he "get into it"
at the party?

323
00:14:56.046 --> 00:14:57.578
Oh. my God!

324
00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:58.746
Come on. Dad!

325
00:14:58.748 --> 00:15:00.548
RICHARD: <i>Wouldn't leave
him alone. the poor guy.</i>

326
00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:02.084
<i>Harlan finally had
to give him the hook.</i>

327
00:15:02.086 --> 00:15:03.718
WALT: The Netflix guys.
their business affair guy...

328
00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.187
RICHARD: <i>I didn't hear
what he said.</i>

329
00:15:05.189 --> 00:15:07.689
<i>but he must've really
handed him his lunch.</i>

330
00:15:07.691 --> 00:15:11.260
<i>'Cause Walt was like a wounded
puppy the rest of the night.</i>

331
00:15:11.262 --> 00:15:12.794
What? Richard said what?

332
00:15:12.796 --> 00:15:14.796
No. Jesus.
We did not get "into it."

333
00:15:14.798 --> 00:15:18.300
I'm just trying to get
an accurate impression.

334
00:15:18.302 --> 00:15:20.668
Harlan took you aside
at the party.

335
00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.740
When you returned.
you were chastened.

336
00:15:26.609 --> 00:15:28.545
What did Harlan say to you?

337
00:15:30.013 --> 00:15:32.247
The Netflix guys.
their business affair guy.

338
00:15:32.249 --> 00:15:34.183
He sent something over.
It's hard numbers this time.

339
00:15:34.185 --> 00:15:35.950
and I just think
this is a window

340
00:15:35.952 --> 00:15:37.719
that's not
gonna stay open.

341
00:15:37.721 --> 00:15:38.820
We need to take
advantage of it

342
00:15:38.822 --> 00:15:40.822
and then you just need
to look at the numbers!

343
00:15:40.824 --> 00:15:42.857
- Yeah. Walt. look...
- Dad! Dad!

344
00:15:42.859 --> 00:15:45.727
You... You put me
in charge of our books.

345
00:15:45.729 --> 00:15:48.629
Let me be in charge!
Let me do this! Please!

346
00:15:48.631 --> 00:15:50.999
They're not
our books. son.

347
00:15:51.001 --> 00:15:53.135
They're my books.

348
00:15:53.137 --> 00:15:56.271
And this is not how I wanted
to have this conversation.

349
00:15:56.273 --> 00:15:58.806
But you're right.
you're right.

350
00:15:58.808 --> 00:16:02.844
It's unfair of me
to keep you tethered

351
00:16:02.846 --> 00:16:05.747
to something that
isn't yours to control.

352
00:16:05.749 --> 00:16:06.814
What?

353
00:16:06.816 --> 00:16:10.553
No. I've done you
a grave disservice.

354
00:16:11.255 --> 00:16:13.188
All these years.

355
00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:15.857
I've kept you
from building something

356
00:16:15.859 --> 00:16:18.195
of your own
that was yours.

357
00:16:20.131 --> 00:16:22.797
But you're not
going to be running

358
00:16:22.799 --> 00:16:25.136
the publishing house
anymore.

359
00:16:25.902 --> 00:16:27.003
You're free of it.

360
00:16:28.004 --> 00:16:29.005
Whoa...

361
00:16:30.707 --> 00:16:32.341
Dad. are you
firing me?

362
00:16:32.343 --> 00:16:34.609
No... (CHUCKLES)

363
00:16:34.611 --> 00:16:36.147
We'll talk
details tomorrow.

364
00:16:37.181 --> 00:16:38.615
My mind's made up.

365
00:16:40.184 --> 00:16:41.185
Good boy.

366
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.862
We talked. We had a business
discussion about e-books.

367
00:16:54.165 --> 00:16:56.067
Jesus. It was nothing.

368
00:16:57.334 --> 00:16:58.866
You want to talk
about an argument.

369
00:16:58.868 --> 00:17:00.768
hell. Ransom had
an argument with him.

370
00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:01.936
Ransom. that's. uh.

371
00:17:01.938 --> 00:17:04.772
- Richard and Linda's son?
- WALT: Mmm.

372
00:17:04.774 --> 00:17:07.744
Look. we all love Ransom.
he's a good kid. We love him.

373
00:17:09.846 --> 00:17:10.945
But?

374
00:17:10.947 --> 00:17:13.348
But he's always been
the black sheep of the family.

375
00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:14.416
Ah.

376
00:17:14.418 --> 00:17:16.051
(STUTTERS)
And I'm not trying to...

377
00:17:16.053 --> 00:17:18.220
I like to keep stuff like this
in the family.

378
00:17:18.222 --> 00:17:21.123
But with Ransom.
he's never had a job.

379
00:17:21.125 --> 00:17:23.825
And Dad.
for some unknown reason.

380
00:17:23.827 --> 00:17:25.294
always supported him.

381
00:17:25.296 --> 00:17:28.665
They have this love-hate bond.
They fight.

382
00:17:29.833 --> 00:17:32.203
But that night. God.
they had a blowout.

383
00:17:32.902 --> 00:17:34.069
About what?

384
00:17:34.071 --> 00:17:35.903
RANSOM:
Are you goddamn insane?

385
00:17:35.905 --> 00:17:37.239
WALT: <i>We couldn't
make it out really.</i>

386
00:17:37.241 --> 00:17:39.040
<i>but it was huge.</i>

387
00:17:39.042 --> 00:17:42.144
<i>And it's strange they went
into another room to do it.</i>

388
00:17:42.146 --> 00:17:44.379
<i>Usually they like
to stoke up drama</i>

389
00:17:44.381 --> 00:17:46.681
<i>in front of the whole family.</i>

390
00:17:46.683 --> 00:17:48.117
Speaking of getting into it...

391
00:17:48.119 --> 00:17:49.518
(CHUCKLES)

392
00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.988
You were at the house early.
to help the caterers set up. Did...

393
00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:57.426
Did you converse with Harlan
at that time?

394
00:17:57.428 --> 00:17:59.894
Well. he was there.
We must have spoke.

395
00:17:59.896 --> 00:18:01.132
In his study?

396
00:18:03.334 --> 00:18:05.300
I don't think so.

397
00:18:05.302 --> 00:18:08.370
You see. I spoke
with the caterer this morning.

398
00:18:08.372 --> 00:18:11.140
she didn't see you
helping her staff.

399
00:18:11.142 --> 00:18:13.841
She did hear Harlan
in a screaming match

400
00:18:13.843 --> 00:18:16.213
with somebody that afternoon
in his study.

401
00:18:17.046 --> 00:18:18.380
Yeah. I don't...

402
00:18:18.382 --> 00:18:20.184
- Screaming match?
- Mmm-hmm.

403
00:18:21.185 --> 00:18:22.351
No.

404
00:18:22.353 --> 00:18:23.784
Um... (CLICKS TONGUE)

405
00:18:23.786 --> 00:18:25.187
But Joni was here. too.

406
00:18:25.189 --> 00:18:27.788
Um. she was early.
so it might have been her.

407
00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:28.923
You can maybe ask her.

408
00:18:28.925 --> 00:18:31.093
These were two male voices.

409
00:18:31.095 --> 00:18:33.027
<i>Harlan shouted the phrase...</i>

410
00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:35.232
HARLAN:
You tell her or I will!

411
00:18:35.932 --> 00:18:37.201
"You tell her

412
00:18:38.302 --> 00:18:39.702
"or I will!"

413
00:18:41.771 --> 00:18:43.039
Bells ringing?

414
00:18:51.948 --> 00:18:53.382
That's none
of your business.

415
00:18:53.384 --> 00:18:54.383
You stay out
of my marriage.

416
00:18:54.385 --> 00:18:57.519
I know my daughter.
and she would want to know.

417
00:18:57.521 --> 00:19:00.255
I've put all of it
in this letter to her.

418
00:19:00.257 --> 00:19:01.923
Tomorrow. she gets it.

419
00:19:01.925 --> 00:19:03.791
Harlan. I'm warning you.

420
00:19:03.793 --> 00:19:05.327
- No. she deserves to know.
- You stay out of my marriage.

421
00:19:05.329 --> 00:19:07.429
She deserves to know.
and you're gonna tell her.

422
00:19:07.431 --> 00:19:10.267
- The hell I am!
- You tell her or I will!

423
00:19:13.237 --> 00:19:15.105
Yes. I know.

424
00:19:16.906 --> 00:19:17.972
Yes.

425
00:19:17.974 --> 00:19:20.841
(CHUCKLES) Uh...

426
00:19:20.843 --> 00:19:25.480
Harlan had finally decided to
put his mom in a nursing home

427
00:19:25.482 --> 00:19:27.882
and Linda had
always opposed that.

428
00:19:27.884 --> 00:19:29.251
And I wanted to wait
until we got back

429
00:19:29.253 --> 00:19:31.286
to Boston. uh. to tell Linda.

430
00:19:31.288 --> 00:19:34.156
so. to avoid a whole scene.

431
00:19:34.158 --> 00:19:36.993
and Harlan wanted me
to tell her then.

432
00:19:38.062 --> 00:19:40.128
That was it.
(INHALES SHARPLY)

433
00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.432
Sorry. Forgot.

434
00:19:42.799 --> 00:19:44.299
The house?

435
00:19:44.301 --> 00:19:47.835
Uh. early.
Richard said you were there.

436
00:19:47.837 --> 00:19:50.006
I was at the house early.

437
00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:52.176
BENOIT: To see Harlan?

438
00:19:53.544 --> 00:19:54.844
To see Harlan.

439
00:19:55.379 --> 00:19:56.779
Yes.

440
00:19:57.814 --> 00:20:00.282
What were you
seeing Harlan about?

441
00:20:00.284 --> 00:20:02.917
It was just a mix-up
with the. uh.

442
00:20:02.919 --> 00:20:04.986
the payment for Meg's tuition.

443
00:20:04.988 --> 00:20:06.255
I'm... I'm...

444
00:20:06.257 --> 00:20:07.924
I'm sorry to press.

445
00:20:09.159 --> 00:20:11.061
but what kind of mix-up?

446
00:20:12.862 --> 00:20:14.329
Yeah. the school hasn't
got the check yet.

447
00:20:14.331 --> 00:20:16.365
I don't know why Alan
didn't mail it.

448
00:20:16.367 --> 00:20:17.999
HARLAN: Well.
Alan didn't mail it

449
00:20:18.001 --> 00:20:21.203
because he caught
a discrepancy.

450
00:20:21.205 --> 00:20:25.274
Alan's office has been wiring
tuition directly to the school

451
00:20:25.276 --> 00:20:26.974
as per your request.

452
00:20:26.976 --> 00:20:30.312
But Phyllis's office that
handles your yearly allowance

453
00:20:30.314 --> 00:20:34.118
has been wiring tuition monies
directly to you as well.

454
00:20:35.252 --> 00:20:38.053
You have been double-dipping
Meg's tuition

455
00:20:38.055 --> 00:20:39.388
and stealing from me.

456
00:20:39.390 --> 00:20:42.357
- (SCOFFS)
- $100.000 a year.

457
00:20:42.359 --> 00:20:44.226
for the past four years.

458
00:20:44.228 --> 00:20:46.295
Harlan. I don't know
how this mix-up happened.

459
00:20:46.297 --> 00:20:47.928
but I swear to God...

460
00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:49.864
HARLAN: So. now I am writing
this tuition check.

461
00:20:49.866 --> 00:20:52.267
but you must know
that this is the last money

462
00:20:52.269 --> 00:20:55.537
you or Meg will get from me.

463
00:20:55.539 --> 00:20:57.205
Please.
you don't understand...

464
00:20:57.207 --> 00:20:59.006
Joni. I know it'll hurt.

465
00:20:59.008 --> 00:21:00.910
but it's all for the best.

466
00:21:02.446 --> 00:21:03.980
My mind's made up.

467
00:21:06.983 --> 00:21:09.451
It was. uh.
a money wiring issue

468
00:21:09.453 --> 00:21:11.153
with the office at the school.

469
00:21:11.155 --> 00:21:14.256
So I had to ask Harlan to cut
a check for the semester.

470
00:21:14.258 --> 00:21:15.559
Mmm. No big deal.

471
00:21:16.493 --> 00:21:17.559
Well...

472
00:21:17.561 --> 00:21:19.261
Why don't we.
uh. just take

473
00:21:19.263 --> 00:21:20.462
a little break
and we'll resu...

474
00:21:20.464 --> 00:21:22.029
Oh. no...

475
00:21:22.031 --> 00:21:23.133
She's gone.

476
00:21:29.206 --> 00:21:30.971
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

477
00:21:30.973 --> 00:21:32.176
LINDA: Richard!

478
00:21:33.477 --> 00:21:35.009
Joni. have you
seen Richard?

479
00:21:35.011 --> 00:21:36.545
No. I was. uh.
just done with the. um...

480
00:21:36.547 --> 00:21:37.614
Okay. thanks.

481
00:21:39.383 --> 00:21:40.384
No.

482
00:21:41.185 --> 00:21:42.852
LINDA: Damn it. Richard!

483
00:21:44.954 --> 00:21:46.022
Richard?

484
00:22:11.315 --> 00:22:13.550
(CHUCKLES)

485
00:22:15.519 --> 00:22:17.388
Son of a bitch.

486
00:22:27.698 --> 00:22:30.732
See. I might be a victim
of my own expectation here.

487
00:22:30.734 --> 00:22:32.967
but when
the great Benoit Blanc

488
00:22:32.969 --> 00:22:34.469
comes knocking
at my door.

489
00:22:34.471 --> 00:22:36.505
I expect it's going
to be about something.

490
00:22:36.507 --> 00:22:38.306
if not extraordinary.

491
00:22:38.308 --> 00:22:40.642
then at least interesting.

492
00:22:40.644 --> 00:22:41.610
But... I'm sorry.

493
00:22:41.612 --> 00:22:45.045
this is an open-and-shut
case of suicide

494
00:22:45.047 --> 00:22:46.581
and. uh. quite frankly. Benny.
we're getting to the point

495
00:22:46.583 --> 00:22:48.316
where I need to know
what we're doing here.

496
00:22:48.318 --> 00:22:49.319
BENOIT: The method?

497
00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:52.289
Throat slit?

498
00:22:53.223 --> 00:22:54.689
Typical for
a suicide?

499
00:22:54.691 --> 00:22:56.625
Yes. I mean.
that's dramatic.

500
00:22:56.627 --> 00:22:58.627
But look around.

501
00:22:58.629 --> 00:23:01.331
I mean. the guy practically
lives in a Clue board.

502
00:23:08.238 --> 00:23:10.472
ELLIOTT: <i>Come on. Benny.
talk to me. all right?</i>

503
00:23:10.474 --> 00:23:13.141
<i>Now. you tell me to invite
all of these people back</i>

504
00:23:13.143 --> 00:23:15.710
<i>for questioning
all over again. I get it.</i>

505
00:23:15.712 --> 00:23:17.145
WAGNER: <i>Listen.
I've had boots on the ground</i>

506
00:23:17.147 --> 00:23:18.280
<i>in this county
for a while now.</i>

507
00:23:18.282 --> 00:23:19.548
<i>People are generally
what they seem to be.</i>

508
00:23:19.550 --> 00:23:21.583
<i>You're not gonna find
murderers in this family.</i>

509
00:23:21.585 --> 00:23:23.017
ELLIOTT:
<i>This is a pleasant family</i>

510
00:23:23.019 --> 00:23:24.252
<i>with the usual quarrels.</i>

511
00:23:24.254 --> 00:23:26.288
<i>but no possible motives
for murder.</i>

512
00:23:26.290 --> 00:23:27.357
<i>Where are you going?</i>

513
00:23:30.093 --> 00:23:31.161
(GASPS)

514
00:23:32.329 --> 00:23:35.363
Harlan Thrombey's nurse.
Marta...

515
00:23:35.365 --> 00:23:37.098
- Cabrera.
- Marta Cabrera. Please.

516
00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.567
Miss Cabrera.
you can just wait inside

517
00:23:38.569 --> 00:23:40.237
- and we'll be with you in...
- BENOIT: Miss Cabrera.

518
00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:46.141
I've been doin'
a little pokin'.

519
00:23:46.143 --> 00:23:48.042
You were hired
on a part-time basis

520
00:23:48.044 --> 00:23:49.678
as a registered
nurse. yes?

521
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.347
Uh. yes. I don't work for a VNA.

522
00:23:52.349 --> 00:23:54.115
Harlan hired
me directly.

523
00:23:54.117 --> 00:23:56.151
Take a seat. please.

524
00:23:56.153 --> 00:23:58.455
And you're paid
a flat rate

525
00:23:59.756 --> 00:24:01.323
for how many hours a week?

526
00:24:01.325 --> 00:24:02.557
Um...

527
00:24:02.559 --> 00:24:05.562
Well. I started at 15.
and then he...

528
00:24:06.663 --> 00:24:07.829
He needed more help.

529
00:24:07.831 --> 00:24:09.500
Medical help?

530
00:24:11.835 --> 00:24:13.504
He needed a friend.

531
00:24:15.839 --> 00:24:20.542
Does having a kind heart
make you a good nurse?

532
00:24:20.544 --> 00:24:22.377
ELLIOTT: All right. Blanc.
I mean. this is...

533
00:24:22.379 --> 00:24:24.546
Yeah. yeah. Marta?
We were just discussing

534
00:24:24.548 --> 00:24:26.748
possible motives
in the family.

535
00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:29.284
I suspect that
Harlan has told you

536
00:24:29.286 --> 00:24:31.653
much unfiltered truth
about each of 'em.

537
00:24:31.655 --> 00:24:35.090
And a little bird
has told me.

538
00:24:35.092 --> 00:24:37.261
how shall I
put this delicately...

539
00:24:38.295 --> 00:24:42.430
You have
a regurgitative reaction

540
00:24:42.432 --> 00:24:44.301
to mistruthin'.
(CHUCKLES)

541
00:24:45.402 --> 00:24:46.835
Who told you that?

542
00:24:46.837 --> 00:24:48.470
Is it true?

543
00:24:48.472 --> 00:24:49.506
Uh...

544
00:24:50.707 --> 00:24:52.274
- Yes.
- Oh.

545
00:24:52.276 --> 00:24:54.776
It's something
I've had since I was a kid.

546
00:24:54.778 --> 00:24:57.145
It's a physical thing
that I... (SHUDDERS)

547
00:24:57.147 --> 00:24:58.580
Just the thought of lying...

548
00:24:58.582 --> 00:25:01.249
Yeah. it makes me puke.

549
00:25:01.251 --> 00:25:02.617
BENOIT: Really?

550
00:25:02.619 --> 00:25:03.685
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

551
00:25:03.687 --> 00:25:05.322
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

552
00:25:06.523 --> 00:25:08.692
Is Richard havin' an affair?

553
00:25:11.895 --> 00:25:13.228
(SIGHS)

554
00:25:13.230 --> 00:25:14.663
Why do men instinctively

555
00:25:14.665 --> 00:25:18.235
pull at loose threads
on their parachutes?

556
00:25:19.469 --> 00:25:20.470
What?

557
00:25:28.178 --> 00:25:29.244
Richard?

558
00:25:29.246 --> 00:25:30.380
Mmm-hmm.

559
00:25:31.548 --> 00:25:33.483
- An affair?
- Yeah.

560
00:25:34.318 --> 00:25:36.353
A yes or no will do.

561
00:25:38.622 --> 00:25:40.288
Mmm... No.

562
00:25:40.290 --> 00:25:41.423
(CLICKS TONGUE)

563
00:25:41.425 --> 00:25:42.490
(SCOFFS)

564
00:25:42.492 --> 00:25:44.225
- (STOMACH GURGLES)
- (GAGS)

565
00:25:44.227 --> 00:25:45.794
- Oh. shit!
- (RETCHES)

566
00:25:45.796 --> 00:25:47.262
- WAGNER: Oh. my God!
- Dear girl. I'm sorry.

567
00:25:47.264 --> 00:25:49.764
- I assumed you were speaking figuratively.
- WAGNER: Here. have some water.

568
00:25:49.766 --> 00:25:52.167
- I have Wet-Naps in the car.
- All right. here. here.

569
00:25:52.169 --> 00:25:53.635
Just take a
sip of this.

570
00:25:53.637 --> 00:25:54.903
Take that.

571
00:25:54.905 --> 00:25:57.205
- That's quite somethin'.
- Hmm?

572
00:25:57.207 --> 00:25:59.574
- Thanks.
- But I was obviously right.

573
00:25:59.576 --> 00:26:01.176
Richard is having
an affair.

574
00:26:01.178 --> 00:26:03.411
His father-in-law found
out and confronted him.

575
00:26:03.413 --> 00:26:04.679
"You tell her
or I will."

576
00:26:04.681 --> 00:26:06.348
Okay. but even if
that were the case. he...

577
00:26:06.350 --> 00:26:07.616
- (MARTA GAGS)
- You all right?

578
00:26:07.618 --> 00:26:08.683
Yeah.

579
00:26:08.685 --> 00:26:09.751
Even if that were
the case. I mean.

580
00:26:09.753 --> 00:26:11.519
protecting a relationship
as a motive.

581
00:26:11.521 --> 00:26:13.254
that's weak sauce.
You know that.

582
00:26:13.256 --> 00:26:15.256
Well. then there
is Joni.

583
00:26:15.258 --> 00:26:16.491
- Joni?
- Joni?

584
00:26:16.493 --> 00:26:17.892
Lifestyle guru Joni?

585
00:26:17.894 --> 00:26:19.494
No. Harlan was supporting
her and her daughter

586
00:26:19.496 --> 00:26:20.695
and that's the
opposite of a motive.

587
00:26:20.697 --> 00:26:22.330
And if that support
was threatened...

588
00:26:22.332 --> 00:26:23.598
Miss Cabrera.
one moment. please.

589
00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:24.933
Yes. I just wanna
get some Scope.

590
00:26:24.935 --> 00:26:26.201
Miss Cabrera...

591
00:26:26.203 --> 00:26:27.369
(DOOR CLOSES)

592
00:26:27.371 --> 00:26:30.807
Was Harlan plannin' on
cutting off Joni's allowance?

593
00:26:33.577 --> 00:26:35.312
Oh. Joni.

594
00:26:36.647 --> 00:26:37.714
What's up?

595
00:26:39.850 --> 00:26:41.216
(STOMACH GURGLES)

596
00:26:41.218 --> 00:26:42.283
Oh. my God.

597
00:26:42.285 --> 00:26:43.385
All right. don't answer that

598
00:26:43.387 --> 00:26:44.686
if you're gonna
puke again. please.

599
00:26:44.688 --> 00:26:46.588
Meg said he paid
the school directly.

600
00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:48.325
Joni said he sent
the money to her.

601
00:26:48.825 --> 00:26:50.458
Both were true.

602
00:26:50.460 --> 00:26:52.427
She was pocketing
the double payment.

603
00:26:52.429 --> 00:26:53.495
Harlan found out.

604
00:26:53.497 --> 00:26:54.963
and cut her off
without a cent.

605
00:26:54.965 --> 00:26:55.964
Yes?

606
00:26:55.966 --> 00:26:59.567
WAGNER: So she bumps him off
for the inheritance?

607
00:26:59.569 --> 00:27:01.503
Come on. no.
have you seen her Insta?

608
00:27:01.505 --> 00:27:02.637
She's an influencer.

609
00:27:02.639 --> 00:27:04.472
No. allowance
as a motive?

610
00:27:04.474 --> 00:27:05.907
Again. more weak sauce.

611
00:27:05.909 --> 00:27:07.709
You're just dumpin' that vat
of weak sauce on me.

612
00:27:07.711 --> 00:27:09.713
Granted. But she
lied to me.

613
00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:11.880
All three of them did.

614
00:27:11.882 --> 00:27:12.883
ELLIOTT: Three?

615
00:27:14.518 --> 00:27:15.750
Walter.

616
00:27:15.752 --> 00:27:18.253
Ah. I see where you're
going with this.

617
00:27:18.255 --> 00:27:20.955
Harlan had turned Walter down
before regarding film rights.

618
00:27:20.957 --> 00:27:23.558
but that night. somethin'
Harlan said shook him.

619
00:27:23.560 --> 00:27:25.326
Now we look at the pattern.

620
00:27:25.328 --> 00:27:27.197
Harlan was cleanin' house.

621
00:27:28.031 --> 00:27:29.232
No wonder.

622
00:27:30.467 --> 00:27:31.900
Did he plan to fire Walter?

623
00:27:31.902 --> 00:27:33.268
Can I just wait inside?

624
00:27:33.270 --> 00:27:34.335
I feel like
I shouldn't be here.

625
00:27:34.337 --> 00:27:35.537
Yeah. please.
just wait inside.

626
00:27:35.539 --> 00:27:36.873
Stay close. all right?

627
00:27:38.008 --> 00:27:39.576
(DOOR OPENS)

628
00:27:40.510 --> 00:27:41.476
(DOOR CLOSES)

629
00:27:41.478 --> 00:27:43.780
BENOIT: You have been
very patient. my friend.

630
00:27:44.715 --> 00:27:45.716
And yes.

631
00:27:46.483 --> 00:27:47.549
you are right.

632
00:27:47.551 --> 00:27:49.951
None of these weak alibis
and domestic squibbles

633
00:27:49.953 --> 00:27:51.686
answer your question...

634
00:27:51.688 --> 00:27:54.889
"Why is Benoit Blanc here?"

635
00:27:54.891 --> 00:27:56.860
Well. now I will tell you why.

636
00:27:57.894 --> 00:27:59.861
I'm here because this mornin'.

637
00:27:59.863 --> 00:28:02.566
someone dodged
a very important question.

638
00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:04.801
Who?

639
00:28:05.535 --> 00:28:07.069
Me.

640
00:28:07.071 --> 00:28:09.537
Linda asked
who hired me.

641
00:28:09.539 --> 00:28:10.974
Well. who hired you?

642
00:28:11.742 --> 00:28:14.442
I do not know.

643
00:28:14.444 --> 00:28:17.378
An envelope of cash showed up
at my apartment yesterday

644
00:28:17.380 --> 00:28:19.547
with a news clippin'
of Thrombey's death.

645
00:28:19.549 --> 00:28:20.917
An envelope?
That worked?

646
00:28:22.686 --> 00:28:25.720
- An envelope of cash.
- Hmm.

647
00:28:25.722 --> 00:28:28.057
So somebody
suspects foul play

648
00:28:28.059 --> 00:28:31.392
and goes through this
ha cha dance of hiring me.

649
00:28:31.394 --> 00:28:32.763
of staying anonymous.

650
00:28:33.563 --> 00:28:35.832
It makes no damn sense.

651
00:28:37.701 --> 00:28:39.002
Compels me. though.

652
00:28:40.937 --> 00:28:43.037
Walk me through
everyone's whereabouts

653
00:28:43.039 --> 00:28:44.040
at the time of death.

654
00:28:45.008 --> 00:28:48.810
We know that the party ended
around 11:30.

655
00:28:48.812 --> 00:28:49.744
- HARLAN: Good night. Joni.
- 'Night.

656
00:28:49.746 --> 00:28:51.579
ELLIOTT:
<i>Marta took Harlan upstairs</i>

657
00:28:51.581 --> 00:28:52.747
<i>to give him his meds.</i>

658
00:28:52.749 --> 00:28:54.516
(STAIRS CREAKING)

659
00:28:54.518 --> 00:28:57.086
<i>The stairs leading
up to Harlan's bedroom</i>

660
00:28:57.088 --> 00:28:59.621
<i>and his attic office
creak horribly</i>

661
00:28:59.623 --> 00:29:01.623
<i>and Linda is a light sleeper.</i>

662
00:29:01.625 --> 00:29:02.624
<i>So we know every time</i>

663
00:29:02.626 --> 00:29:04.659
<i>someone took the stairs
that night.</i>

664
00:29:04.661 --> 00:29:07.495
(CHANTING IN HINDI)

665
00:29:07.497 --> 00:29:09.831
ELLIOTT: <i>The first was
when Joni heard a ka-thunk</i>

666
00:29:09.833 --> 00:29:11.733
<i>from somewhere above her
in the house.</i>

667
00:29:11.735 --> 00:29:12.967
(LOUD THUD)

668
00:29:12.969 --> 00:29:14.037
(SIGHS)

669
00:29:20.944 --> 00:29:22.544
<i>She's concerned about Harlan.</i>

670
00:29:22.546 --> 00:29:24.712
<i>so she goes up
to investigate...</i>

671
00:29:24.714 --> 00:29:25.980
(STAIRS CREAKING)

672
00:29:25.982 --> 00:29:27.982
<i>Waking Linda.</i>

673
00:29:27.984 --> 00:29:30.451
<i>Harlan was in his attic office
with Marta.</i>

674
00:29:30.453 --> 00:29:31.853
- Hi. Joni.
- I just... Hi.

675
00:29:31.855 --> 00:29:32.987
ELLIOTT: <i>He explained that
they had just</i>

676
00:29:32.989 --> 00:29:33.922
<i>knocked over the Go board.</i>

677
00:29:33.924 --> 00:29:35.291
I just knocked over
the Go board. so...

678
00:29:35.293 --> 00:29:37.659
ELLIOTT: <i>You know. that game
with the grid and stones?</i>

679
00:29:37.661 --> 00:29:38.893
<i>They play it every night.</i>

680
00:29:38.895 --> 00:29:40.129
<i>He was fine. "Go to bed."</i>

681
00:29:40.131 --> 00:29:41.729
Go to bed. Joni.

682
00:29:41.731 --> 00:29:43.165
- Love you. 'Night.
- Love you.

683
00:29:43.167 --> 00:29:44.801
- ELLIOTT: <i>So she did.</i>
- Bye.

684
00:29:45.702 --> 00:29:47.035
ELLIOTT: <i>Ten minutes later.</i>

685
00:29:47.037 --> 00:29:48.970
<i>Linda is awoken
a second time...</i>

686
00:29:48.972 --> 00:29:51.173
(STAIRS CREAKING)

687
00:29:51.175 --> 00:29:52.507
<i>By Marta leaving.</i>

688
00:29:52.509 --> 00:29:54.442
MARTA: Walt. I'm leaving.

689
00:29:54.444 --> 00:29:57.045
<i>Walt was smokin' a cigar
on the porch with his son.</i>

690
00:29:57.047 --> 00:29:59.015
<i>He saw her leave
and drive off.</i>

691
00:30:00.051 --> 00:30:01.516
<i>Noted the time.</i>

692
00:30:01.518 --> 00:30:02.784
<i>Midnight.</i>

693
00:30:02.786 --> 00:30:04.153
(CAR DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)

694
00:30:04.155 --> 00:30:05.689
(ENGINE STARTS)

695
00:30:08.992 --> 00:30:10.259
<i>Fifteen minutes later.</i>

696
00:30:10.261 --> 00:30:13.027
<i>Linda is awoken for the third
and final time...</i>

697
00:30:13.029 --> 00:30:15.830
(STAIRS CREAKING)

698
00:30:15.832 --> 00:30:17.999
<i>By someone coming
down the stairs.</i>

699
00:30:18.001 --> 00:30:20.602
<i>Harlan. who came down
for a midnight snack.</i>

700
00:30:20.604 --> 00:30:22.137
WALT: Dad. go back to bed.

701
00:30:22.139 --> 00:30:24.141
ELLIOTT: <i>Which Walt tried
to discourage.</i>

702
00:30:25.008 --> 00:30:26.275
<i>Based on this.</i>

703
00:30:26.277 --> 00:30:28.077
<i>the medical examiner
determined the time of death</i>

704
00:30:28.079 --> 00:30:31.080
<i>to be between
12:15 and 2.00 a.m.</i>

705
00:30:31.082 --> 00:30:32.881
<i>As Walt was
finishing his cigar</i>

706
00:30:32.883 --> 00:30:34.983
<i>at about 12:30. Meg came home.</i>

707
00:30:34.985 --> 00:30:36.718
<i>She went straight to bed.</i>

708
00:30:36.720 --> 00:30:39.621
<i>Walt and Jacob
turned in shortly after that.</i>

709
00:30:39.623 --> 00:30:41.090
- (SNORING)
- (DOGS BARKING)

710
00:30:41.092 --> 00:30:43.458
<i>And sometime later that night.</i>

711
00:30:43.460 --> 00:30:46.494
<i>it's undetermined.
but possibly near 3:00 a.m..</i>

712
00:30:46.496 --> 00:30:49.697
<i>Meg woke up because
the dogs were barking outside.</i>

713
00:30:49.699 --> 00:30:52.734
<i>She used the bathroom.
went back to bed.</i>

714
00:30:52.736 --> 00:30:54.636
That's it. All right?

715
00:30:54.638 --> 00:30:56.704
Now. everyone's
stories matched.

716
00:30:56.706 --> 00:30:58.441
every moment
accounted for.

717
00:30:59.143 --> 00:31:01.476
And there is
no other staircase

718
00:31:01.478 --> 00:31:02.677
up to Harlan's room?

719
00:31:02.679 --> 00:31:04.579
None. Just the creaky one.

720
00:31:04.581 --> 00:31:05.580
Interesting.

721
00:31:05.582 --> 00:31:08.683
WAGNER: So. uh. we know that
Ransom didn't do it

722
00:31:08.685 --> 00:31:09.984
because he
wasn't there.

723
00:31:09.986 --> 00:31:11.552
Marta couldn't have.

724
00:31:11.554 --> 00:31:13.222
Harlan was still alive
when she left.

725
00:31:13.224 --> 00:31:14.856
- Yeah.
- Meg...

726
00:31:14.858 --> 00:31:16.591
Meg came home
during the window

727
00:31:16.593 --> 00:31:17.659
- of the time of death. right?
- ELLIOTT: Now look. look. it was a...

728
00:31:17.661 --> 00:31:19.694
Except it was a suicide.
all right?

729
00:31:19.696 --> 00:31:21.796
Harlan slit right
through his carotid.

730
00:31:21.798 --> 00:31:23.598
We saw from
the blood splat patterns

731
00:31:23.600 --> 00:31:24.999
that they
were uninterrupted.

732
00:31:25.001 --> 00:31:27.035
meaning. it's almost
impossible for anyone

733
00:31:27.037 --> 00:31:29.871
to have been around him
at the time.

734
00:31:29.873 --> 00:31:31.173
He's the one who cut his
own throat. all right?

735
00:31:31.175 --> 00:31:32.740
I don't know why
we keep goin' over this.

736
00:31:32.742 --> 00:31:35.144
Physical evidence
can tell a clear story

737
00:31:35.146 --> 00:31:36.780
with a forked tongue.

738
00:31:37.547 --> 00:31:38.414
What?

739
00:31:38.416 --> 00:31:40.848
And as we can see
from this mornin'.

740
00:31:40.850 --> 00:31:42.617
everyone can lie.

741
00:31:42.619 --> 00:31:44.286
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

742
00:31:44.288 --> 00:31:45.687
Well.

743
00:31:45.689 --> 00:31:47.056
almost everyone.

744
00:31:47.058 --> 00:31:48.192
