as a suspect.

994
00:42:00.804 --> 00:42:03.206
It sounds crazy.
but it'll work.

995
00:42:06.410 --> 00:42:07.842
(EXHALES)

996
00:42:07.844 --> 00:42:10.581
<i>Walt is smoking outside.
and he'll see you</i>

997
00:42:11.615 --> 00:42:13.248
<i>through the glazed window.</i>

998
00:42:13.250 --> 00:42:15.352
WALT: Dad? Go back to bed.

999
00:42:16.653 --> 00:42:18.320
HARLAN: <i>You were seen leaving.</i>

1000
00:42:18.322 --> 00:42:21.323
<i>The security cameras
show you driving off.</i>

1001
00:42:21.325 --> 00:42:22.524
<i>And 20 minutes later.</i>

1002
00:42:22.526 --> 00:42:25.527
<i>I'm seen alive and well
by my son.</i>

1003
00:42:25.529 --> 00:42:26.561
(CHUCKLES) <i>You see.</i>

1004
00:42:26.563 --> 00:42:29.197
<i>you've gone from suspect
number one</i>

1005
00:42:29.199 --> 00:42:30.865
<i>to an impossibility.</i>

1006
00:42:30.867 --> 00:42:32.767
<i>Leave the way you came</i>

1007
00:42:32.769 --> 00:42:35.606
<i>and don't be seen.</i>

1008
00:42:37.207 --> 00:42:38.275
(GASPS SOFTLY)

1009
00:42:42.279 --> 00:42:44.281
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1010
00:42:46.183 --> 00:42:47.484
Ransom?

1011
00:42:48.952 --> 00:42:51.254
Are you back
again already?

1012
00:42:54.658 --> 00:42:56.458
HARLAN: <i>Drive home.</i>

1013
00:42:56.460 --> 00:42:58.560
<i>And sometime
in the next few days</i>

1014
00:42:58.562 --> 00:43:00.695
<i>the police will question you.</i>

1015
00:43:00.697 --> 00:43:03.465
No. No. no. no. No!

1016
00:43:03.467 --> 00:43:05.400
I can't lie!

1017
00:43:05.402 --> 00:43:07.402
You know I can't lie!
I'll puke!

1018
00:43:07.404 --> 00:43:10.238
Well. then don't lie.
Tell fragments of the truth.

1019
00:43:10.240 --> 00:43:11.673
In this exact order.

1020
00:43:11.675 --> 00:43:12.876
(COIN RINGING)

1021
00:43:14.611 --> 00:43:15.712
(RINGING STOPS)

1022
00:43:18.815 --> 00:43:20.384
I took him upstairs.

1023
00:43:21.618 --> 00:43:23.720
We played our nightly
game of Go.

1024
00:43:25.555 --> 00:43:27.956
At some point.
he knocked the board over

1025
00:43:27.958 --> 00:43:31.161
and Joni came up
to check on us.

1026
00:43:31.695 --> 00:43:32.929
Um...

1027
00:43:34.698 --> 00:43:36.433
I gave him pain medication.

1028
00:43:37.434 --> 00:43:39.903
He pulled his shoulder
last week.

1029
00:43:40.370 --> 00:43:41.503
Um...

1030
00:43:41.505 --> 00:43:43.840
And I left him
in his study.

1031
00:43:44.574 --> 00:43:45.840
At midnight

1032
00:43:45.842 --> 00:43:47.244
I said goodbye
to Walt.

1033
00:43:49.413 --> 00:43:50.378
went home.

1034
00:43:50.380 --> 00:43:52.549
What kind of medication
did you give him?

1035
00:43:55.752 --> 00:43:57.686
Since his injury.
I've been giving him

1036
00:43:57.688 --> 00:44:00.855
a 100 milligram IV push
of Toradol.

1037
00:44:00.857 --> 00:44:03.258
It's a non-narcotic analgesic.

1038
00:44:03.260 --> 00:44:04.993
And to help him sleep.

1039
00:44:04.995 --> 00:44:07.595
three milligrams
of morphine.

1040
00:44:07.597 --> 00:44:09.464
ELLIOTT: And the family
was aware of this?

1041
00:44:09.466 --> 00:44:10.799
MARTA: Yes. of course.

1042
00:44:10.801 --> 00:44:12.967
ELLIOTT: Did you notice
anything strange

1043
00:44:12.969 --> 00:44:14.671
or off about his demeanor?

1044
00:44:18.542 --> 00:44:19.576
No.

1045
00:44:21.311 --> 00:44:23.445
(STOMACH GURGLES SOFTLY)

1046
00:44:23.447 --> 00:44:25.515
Well. that sounds
about right.

1047
00:44:26.850 --> 00:44:28.719
Thank you. Miss Cabrera.

1048
00:44:42.066 --> 00:44:43.533
(RETCHING)

1049
00:44:46.937 --> 00:44:49.571
WALT: Hey. sis. people are
gonna start getting here

1050
00:44:49.573 --> 00:44:50.872
- for the memorial pretty soon.
- (SNIFFLES)

1051
00:44:50.874 --> 00:44:51.875
Are you...

1052
00:44:54.377 --> 00:44:56.578
- (SIGHS)
- Are you all right?

1053
00:44:56.580 --> 00:44:58.882
I was just thinking
about Dad's games.

1054
00:45:00.617 --> 00:45:02.552
(EXHALES DEEPLY)
This all feels like one.

1055
00:45:03.553 --> 00:45:06.022
Like something he'd write.
not do.

1056
00:45:07.091 --> 00:45:09.893
I keep waiting for
the big reveal.

1057
00:45:11.762 --> 00:45:14.028
(VOICE BREAKING)
Where it'll make sense.

1058
00:45:14.030 --> 00:45:15.599
Wouldn't that be nice?

1059
00:45:16.733 --> 00:45:17.868
Oh. Walt.

1060
00:45:19.536 --> 00:45:21.035
(SOBBING)

1061
00:45:21.037 --> 00:45:22.873
FRAN: <i>I don't think
he killed himself.</i>

1062
00:45:23.607 --> 00:45:25.673
I don't. I really don't.

1063
00:45:25.675 --> 00:45:27.342
There's this
Hallmark movie

1064
00:45:27.344 --> 00:45:29.644
called <i>Deadly by Surprise</i>
with Danica McKellar.

1065
00:45:29.646 --> 00:45:31.080
And in it. she plays
this wife

1066
00:45:31.082 --> 00:45:33.515
who's getting poisoned
by her husband.

1067
00:45:33.517 --> 00:45:35.117
but he's doing it
little by little.

1068
00:45:35.119 --> 00:45:36.085
so she doesn't know it

1069
00:45:36.087 --> 00:45:38.820
and she goes crazy.
and she kills herself.

1070
00:45:38.822 --> 00:45:40.688
And my cousin.
who's a receptionist

1071
00:45:40.690 --> 00:45:42.457
at the medical
examiner's office.

1072
00:45:42.459 --> 00:45:44.492
she says that stuff
totally happens.

1073
00:45:44.494 --> 00:45:46.027
It's not even 3% as crazy

1074
00:45:46.029 --> 00:45:47.695
as the stuff she's seen
come through there.

1075
00:45:47.697 --> 00:45:48.799
So. I'm just like...

1076
00:45:50.367 --> 00:45:51.966
JONI: Oh. God. yeah!

1077
00:45:51.968 --> 00:45:54.136
I mean. don't like him
because you love him.

1078
00:45:54.138 --> 00:45:57.005
RICHARD: No. I don't like him.
he's an asshole.

1079
00:45:57.007 --> 00:45:59.407
But maybe an asshole
is what we needed.

1080
00:45:59.409 --> 00:46:00.975
Oh. my God. yeah.

1081
00:46:00.977 --> 00:46:02.710
an asshole is what
Germany needed

1082
00:46:02.712 --> 00:46:04.779
- in 1930-whatever.
- RICHARD: Here we go.

1083
00:46:04.781 --> 00:46:06.748
Come on. Joni. those two
things don't even conflate.

1084
00:46:06.750 --> 00:46:08.449
- JONI: There is the problem...
- Oh. Jesus.

1085
00:46:08.451 --> 00:46:09.584
JONI: You do not care
about anybody's feelings...

1086
00:46:09.586 --> 00:46:12.087
I'm gonna disappear until
the politics talk is done.

1087
00:46:12.089 --> 00:46:14.489
- JONI: You. my friend...
- You want some champers?

1088
00:46:14.491 --> 00:46:16.391
I can't.
I'm technically working.

1089
00:46:16.393 --> 00:46:18.127
JONI: Why don't you take off
your red cap. Richard.

1090
00:46:18.129 --> 00:46:19.161
and look around you?

1091
00:46:19.163 --> 00:46:21.629
The streets are literally
flooded with Nazis.

1092
00:46:21.631 --> 00:46:22.664
No. no. no. No. no. no.

1093
00:46:22.666 --> 00:46:25.967
We are losing our way of life
and our culture.

1094
00:46:25.969 --> 00:46:27.001
That's right.

1095
00:46:27.003 --> 00:46:28.703
DONNA: There are millions
of Mexicans coming.

1096
00:46:28.705 --> 00:46:30.105
- Oh. God. really?
- Don't make this a race thing.

1097
00:46:30.107 --> 00:46:31.706
You always make this
a race thing.

1098
00:46:31.708 --> 00:46:33.075
- Yeah. this is not about race.
- I would say the same thing

1099
00:46:33.077 --> 00:46:34.509
if they were
European immigrants.

1100
00:46:34.511 --> 00:46:36.477
Oh. yeah? So. if the
Swiss were. like.

1101
00:46:36.479 --> 00:46:38.513
- clogging in the streets...
- No. No. no. we allow them in

1102
00:46:38.515 --> 00:46:40.748
and they think
they own what's ours.

1103
00:46:40.750 --> 00:46:42.951
They're putting children
in cages!

1104
00:46:42.953 --> 00:46:44.119
- I mean. these are camps!
- Yes.

1105
00:46:44.121 --> 00:46:45.486
RICHARD: Come on. Joni.

1106
00:46:45.488 --> 00:46:46.955
nobody's saying that isn't bad.

1107
00:46:46.957 --> 00:46:48.890
but the parents have
some blame here.

1108
00:46:48.892 --> 00:46:51.626
Oh. for what? For wanting
a better life for their kids?

1109
00:46:51.628 --> 00:46:54.196
- Isn't that what America is...
- For breaking the law!

1110
00:46:54.198 --> 00:46:55.130
(GROANS) My God.

1111
00:46:55.132 --> 00:46:55.997
RICHARD: And you're gonna
hate hearing this.

1112
00:46:55.999 --> 00:46:58.700
but it's true.
America is for Americans.

1113
00:46:58.702 --> 00:46:59.934
JONI: Don't point at me.

1114
00:46:59.936 --> 00:47:01.103
Where's Marta?
Is she still here?

1115
00:47:01.105 --> 00:47:02.637
- LINDA: Oh. God. don't.
- RICHARD: Marta!

1116
00:47:02.639 --> 00:47:03.938
- Come on over.
- No. Richard.

1117
00:47:03.940 --> 00:47:05.207
Come on over. Marta.
Please. come over.

1118
00:47:05.209 --> 00:47:06.474
JONI: You're shitting me.

1119
00:47:06.476 --> 00:47:07.842
Marta.

1120
00:47:07.844 --> 00:47:11.813
your family is from Uruguay.
but you did it right.

1121
00:47:11.815 --> 00:47:14.216
I mean. what I'm saying is
they did it legally.

1122
00:47:14.218 --> 00:47:15.585
She did it the right way.

1123
00:47:16.187 --> 00:47:17.652
You work hard.

1124
00:47:17.654 --> 00:47:20.455
and you'll earn your share
from the ground up.

1125
00:47:20.457 --> 00:47:22.857
Just like Dad
and like all the rest of us.

1126
00:47:22.859 --> 00:47:24.792
And I'll bet you
agree with me. right?

1127
00:47:24.794 --> 00:47:27.062
Oh. just leave the poor girl
alone. Richard.

1128
00:47:27.064 --> 00:47:29.664
It's okay! I just wanna
hear what she has to say!

1129
00:47:29.666 --> 00:47:30.798
It's okay. Marta.
you can speak.

1130
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:32.134
JONI: Oh. sweetheart.
don't feel pressure to answer.

1131
00:47:32.136 --> 00:47:33.768
- This is just a...
- RICHARD: Look...

1132
00:47:33.770 --> 00:47:34.869
- JONI: Please don't.
- If you wanna

1133
00:47:34.871 --> 00:47:36.638
become an American.

1134
00:47:36.640 --> 00:47:39.074
there are legal
ways to do it.

1135
00:47:39.076 --> 00:47:40.608
But if you break the law.

1136
00:47:40.610 --> 00:47:43.044
it doesn't matter
how good your heart is.

1137
00:47:43.046 --> 00:47:45.880
you gotta face
the consequences!

1138
00:47:45.882 --> 00:47:47.515
RANSOM:
Are you goddamn insane?

1139
00:47:47.517 --> 00:47:49.719
- HARLAN: It's done.
- RANSOM: Hey! I'm warning you.

1140
00:47:54.858 --> 00:47:56.758
FRAN: That's when I ask her.
I'm like.

1141
00:47:56.760 --> 00:47:57.926
"Tonya. what is wrong
with people?"

1142
00:47:57.928 --> 00:47:59.627
Literally.

1143
00:47:59.629 --> 00:48:01.996
Oh. my God!
Marta. what?

1144
00:48:01.998 --> 00:48:03.498
- Marta?
- (BREATHING HEAVILY)

1145
00:48:03.500 --> 00:48:04.632
What's the matter?

1146
00:48:04.634 --> 00:48:06.834
Whoa. whoa.
Hey. Breathe.

1147
00:48:06.836 --> 00:48:09.837
- FRAN: Oh. my gosh.
- Marta. are you okay?

1148
00:48:09.839 --> 00:48:12.076
Hey. Fran. do you still
have your stash?

1149
00:48:17.614 --> 00:48:19.047
Take 'em whenever
you need 'em.

1150
00:48:19.049 --> 00:48:21.683
They're just drying out
since you gave me that Juul.

1151
00:48:21.685 --> 00:48:23.052
Thanks. Fran.

1152
00:48:23.054 --> 00:48:24.953
- Hey. Hey.
- I'm sorry.

1153
00:48:24.955 --> 00:48:26.055
- No. just... No. stop...
- I'm sorry.

1154
00:48:26.057 --> 00:48:27.555
I'm just very. very sorry.

1155
00:48:27.557 --> 00:48:29.158
Stop saying
you're sorry. Jesus!

1156
00:48:29.160 --> 00:48:31.293
I hate this. Oh. God.
my heart won't stop...

1157
00:48:31.295 --> 00:48:32.560
I can't...

1158
00:48:32.562 --> 00:48:33.795
(EXHALES)

1159
00:48:33.797 --> 00:48:35.699
It's just everything...
No. thank you.

1160
00:48:38.635 --> 00:48:40.635
That's where Fran
keeps her stash?

1161
00:48:40.637 --> 00:48:42.137
(CHUCKLES)

1162
00:48:42.139 --> 00:48:43.673
Who's gonna
open a clock?

1163
00:48:45.242 --> 00:48:47.276
(LOUDLY) Do you want
dinner. Nana?

1164
00:48:47.278 --> 00:48:49.610
Dinner? To eat?

1165
00:48:49.612 --> 00:48:51.612
- To eat?
- LINDA: Walt?

1166
00:48:51.614 --> 00:48:53.082
- Nana?
- Walt. Walt. she's fine.

1167
00:48:53.084 --> 00:48:55.186
She ate the entire
salmon spread already.

1168
00:48:57.054 --> 00:48:59.821
Walt? Did you tell Marta yet.
what we all talked about?

1169
00:48:59.823 --> 00:49:01.723
No. not yet.
Is now a good time?

1170
00:49:01.725 --> 00:49:03.925
Yes. Yes. a very good
time. right now.

1171
00:49:03.927 --> 00:49:05.260
WALT: Oh. okay.

1172
00:49:05.262 --> 00:49:07.198
All right. Calm down.

1173
00:49:09.599 --> 00:49:11.166
Marta.

1174
00:49:11.168 --> 00:49:13.770
we've been
talking it over and. uh...

1175
00:49:15.239 --> 00:49:18.006
- Have you been smoking grass?
- No.

1176
00:49:18.008 --> 00:49:19.974
- Mmm-hmm.
- Come on.

1177
00:49:19.976 --> 00:49:21.743
Marta. we've been
talking it over.

1178
00:49:21.745 --> 00:49:24.179
and. uh.
the whole family.

1179
00:49:24.181 --> 00:49:26.083
we'd like to take
care of you.

1180
00:49:27.784 --> 00:49:28.885
What does that mean?

1181
00:49:30.087 --> 00:49:32.121
We all think that
you deserve something.

1182
00:49:32.123 --> 00:49:34.722
Financially.
we'd like to help you out.

1183
00:49:34.724 --> 00:49:36.693
You were never anything
but good to Dad

1184
00:49:37.794 --> 00:49:39.529
and because of that we...

1185
00:49:40.197 --> 00:49:41.765
You can count on us.

1186
00:49:42.599 --> 00:49:44.068
- Hmm?
- Yeah.

1187
00:49:46.237 --> 00:49:48.770
I thought you should've been
at the funeral.

1188
00:49:48.772 --> 00:49:50.740
by the way. I was outvoted.

1189
00:49:51.108 --> 00:49:52.176
(CHUCKLES)

1190
00:49:58.249 --> 00:49:59.616
- (LIGHTER CLICKS)
- (GASPS)

1191
00:50:01.718 --> 00:50:02.719
MARTA: Detective.

1192
00:50:04.121 --> 00:50:05.122
You're still here?

1193
00:50:06.756 --> 00:50:07.857
BENOIT: Mmm.

1194
00:50:11.795 --> 00:50:13.628
Did you know Harlan?

1195
00:50:13.630 --> 00:50:14.896
BENOIT: He knew my father.

1196
00:50:14.898 --> 00:50:16.966
who was a police detective
years ago.

1197
00:50:18.001 --> 00:50:19.101
Oh.

1198
00:50:19.103 --> 00:50:21.037
My father
respected Harlan.

1199
00:50:21.771 --> 00:50:23.704
That says quite a lot.

1200
00:50:23.706 --> 00:50:25.041
Is that why
you're here?

1201
00:50:26.377 --> 00:50:28.177
Here now. here?

1202
00:50:28.179 --> 00:50:30.279
(CHUCKLES) No.

1203
00:50:30.281 --> 00:50:32.615
I stayed hoping to speak
to you a little more.

1204
00:50:37.987 --> 00:50:40.990
Something is afoot
with this whole affair.

1205
00:50:42.326 --> 00:50:43.991
I know it.

1206
00:50:43.993 --> 00:50:46.029
I believe you know it. too.

1207
00:50:47.831 --> 00:50:49.166
So you're gonna keep digging?

1208
00:50:50.434 --> 00:50:53.868
Harlan's detectives.
they dig.

1209
00:50:53.870 --> 00:50:56.071
They riffle and root.

1210
00:50:56.073 --> 00:50:57.308
Truffle pigs.

1211
00:50:59.110 --> 00:51:03.080
I anticipate the terminus
of <i>Gravity's Rainbow.</i>

1212
00:51:03.913 --> 00:51:05.082
<i>Gravity's Rainbow?</i>

1213
00:51:05.715 --> 00:51:07.014
It's a novel.

1214
00:51:07.016 --> 00:51:08.850
Yeah. I know.

1215
00:51:08.852 --> 00:51:11.220
- I haven't read it though.
- Neither have I.

1216
00:51:11.222 --> 00:51:12.287
Nobody has.

1217
00:51:12.289 --> 00:51:13.756
But I like the title.

1218
00:51:14.757 --> 00:51:16.891
It describes
the path of a projectile

1219
00:51:16.893 --> 00:51:19.294
determined by natural law.

1220
00:51:19.296 --> 00:51:21.829
<i>Et voila.</i> my method.

1221
00:51:21.831 --> 00:51:23.165
I observe the facts

1222
00:51:23.167 --> 00:51:26.000
without biases
of the head or heart.

1223
00:51:26.002 --> 00:51:28.002
I determine the arc's path.

1224
00:51:28.004 --> 00:51:30.738
stroll leisurely
to its terminus

1225
00:51:30.740 --> 00:51:33.277
and the truth
falls at my feet.

1226
00:51:35.845 --> 00:51:39.148
The medical examiner was ready
to rule this a suicide.

1227
00:51:39.150 --> 00:51:42.186
but Elliott agreed to keep it
pending for 48 hours.

1228
00:51:42.852 --> 00:51:43.918
Tomorrow morning.

1229
00:51:43.920 --> 00:51:45.753
I search the grounds
and the house.

1230
00:51:45.755 --> 00:51:46.890
begin my investigation.

1231
00:51:47.957 --> 00:51:50.125
I want you to be
by my side for it.

1232
00:51:50.127 --> 00:51:51.726
- What?
- My confidante.

1233
00:51:51.728 --> 00:51:52.827
My eyes and ears.

1234
00:51:52.829 --> 00:51:54.762
Hey. Wait. wait.
Detective. Why me?

1235
00:51:54.764 --> 00:51:57.234
I trust your kind heart.

1236
00:51:59.136 --> 00:52:00.135
Also. you're the only one

1237
00:52:00.137 --> 00:52:02.239
